    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The `memberId` change is in place and the full test suite passes: 31 tests, 0 failures.\n\n**What a memberId looks like.** For example `NSW2716E6609E1`, from a real test run: region `NSW`, fiscal year `27`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, check digit `1`. HASH8 is the same SHA-256 over telephone + last name that the region-and-hash identity used before.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **New helper** \u2014 `util/MemberIds.java` builds a memberId and reads the region and fiscal year back out of it. The Luhn check digit calculation moved here from the mapper.\n- **Database and entity** \u2014 the `customer_code` column is now `member_id` in all four database schemas, widened from 20 to 30 characters so `UNKNOWN` plus a suffix still fits. The entity and all repositories now use `memberId`.\n- **Collision handling** \u2014 `ClinicServiceImpl` now checks the memberId for clashes. A clash gets `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 appended after the check digit, as before. If an owner has no registration date, the fiscal year falls back to today.\n- **Removed fields** \u2014 `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` are gone from the API spec (`openapi.yml`), the generated response objects and the mapper.\n- **Values that now come from the memberId:**\n  - `fiscalYear` is read from the memberId's FY part, falling back to the registration date when there's no memberId.\n  - `locality` is read from its region part, and `ownerSegment` uses that locality.\n- **Audit** \u2014 the log line and the `OwnerCreatedEvent` record both carry `memberId`. The log line now shows `fiscalYear` in place of the removed membership number and check digit.\n- **Tests** \u2014 `CustomerCodeCollisionTests` is renamed to `MemberIdCollisionTests` and updated for the new format. I added `MemberIdsTests`, which checks the exact check-digit values.\n\n**Things to be aware of:**\n- **The check digit doesn't cover the suffix.** It's calculated over `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` only, so `NSW\u20264-2` keeps the same check digit as `NSW\u20264`. I read the spec that way; say if you'd rather the suffix be part of the calculation.\n- **Existing data isn't migrated.** I renamed the column in the schema files, but nothing converts existing `customer_code` values. Any real MySQL or Postgres database would need a migration script.\n- **The audit log line changed.** Anything that parses it will need updating.\n\nNothing has been committed. There's no git repository here.",
